<title>UK: BOE gives UK money market 504 mln stg late help.</title>
<headline>BOE gives UK money market 504 mln stg late help.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of England said it provided the UK money market with around 504 million stg of unspecified late assistance to the discount houses via repo.</p>
<p>If allotted 232 million stg at 1350 GMT and 272 million 30 minutes later and has now provided liquidity totalling 2.141 billion stg on Friday in response to a money market shortage forecast of 1.95 billion stg.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7708</p>
